% AUTHOR: implementation-absys (an agent: Claude Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5). One text for absys, absys-depth-first and absys-wake-back.
% PRECURSOR-SEEN: no. Not any E01-E09 program (see programs/absys/README.md, batch 1D, for what was read).
% NAMED VARIANT, not the primary (programs/absys/P13d.ab1 is). Chosen as a variant before any run.
% NOTATION: 1969 (.ab1), the earliest notation with arithmetic (systems/absys/README.md, Notation).
% IDIOM: a relation as name'=lambda x begin {A or B} end, primes for new local names, lists [a;b] and [h&t]: Foster and Elcock 1969 (map and item, examples/map.ab1, examples/triples.ab1);
% IDIOM: a case's head as equations on the lambda's parameters: Elcock 1990 p. 8 (app, examples/append.abs);
% IDIOM: arithmetic as an assertion usable in every direction, a = b + 1: Foster and Elcock 1969 (tutorial ch. 8); Foster 1968, pass sets (docs/decisions.md rule 23);
% IDIOM: begin ... end groups the stage's relations into one conjunction, one assertion: Foster and Elcock 1969 (docs/decisions.md, Three notations).
% PARAMETERS n
% P13d, every instance (P13d.n100 ... P13d.n100000): n is the harness's parameter (README 3.4). Unknowns s, r.
% One stage: range(<k>, n, s) and revacc(s, r), in that order, as one conjunction.
% CONSTANTS BEGIN
rk = 1   % stage 1: range(rk, n, s)
% CONSTANTS END
% REFORMULATION THAT CHANGES THE MEANING (systems/absys/README.md, Notation: calibration's range): case 1's m > n is
% written m = n + 1, and case 2's m <= n is dropped. On range(m, n, s) with m <= n + 1 the solutions are the problem's;
% with m > n + 1 there are none, where the problem has s = <>. Case 2 also applies at m = n + 1 and goes on for ever.
range'=lambda a, b, w
    begin {w = [] a = b + 1 or
           w = [a&t'] a1' = a + 1 range(a1, b, t)} end
% revacc, P13 Vocabulary, its one case: revacc(a, b) if racc(a, <>, b).
revacc'=lambda p, w
    begin racc(p, [], w) end
% racc, P13 Vocabulary, cases 2 and 3 in that order. Case 2: racc(<>, b, b), its head as equations.
% Case 3: its head equation a = <h> ++ t, then racc(t, <h> ++ c, b).
racc'=lambda p, c, w
    begin {p = [] c = w or
           p = [h'&t'] racc(t, [h&c], w)} end
% STAGE 1
begin range(rk, n, s) revacc(s, r) end
